Notable fidelity decisions:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Structs are modelled as flat byte arrays with the exact x86-64 layout ([38;5;10muser_t[0m 72 bytes, [38;5;10mfile_t[0m 612, [38;5;10mvariable_t[0m 160) because the C code [38;5;10mstrcpy[0ms tokens of up to 63 chars into [38;5;10mchar[32][0m fields. A 40-char username really does spill into [38;5;10mpassword[0m, and the C output reflects that; the flat model reproduces it exactly.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mstrcmp[0m/[38;5;10mstrncmp[0m return the unsigned-char difference (glibc behavior), which is observable in [38;5;10mcompare[0m/[38;5;10mcompareN[0m output. [38;5;10matoi[0m follows glibc's [38;5;10mstrtol[0m saturation, and the [38;5;10mint[0m→[38;5;10msize_t[0m sign extension in [38;5;10mstrncmp(a, b, n)[0m is preserved, so [38;5;10mcompareN x y -1[0m behaves like the C version.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfgets[0m is emulated exactly: a line longer than 255 bytes is split, and each chunk gets its own [38;5;10m> [0m prompt with no newline stripped.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mtime[0m/[38;5;10mctime[0m call libc directly (the only [38;5;10munsafe[0m) so timezone handling and format match.[0m[0m
